// Negative autoregulation: an idealized mass-action teaching model.
// Source of the model is the four reactions below; parameters are illustrative,
// not measured or fitted. This is a gene-regulation CRN, not a Seesaw DNA design.
// G = free promoter, R = promoter with a bound repressor, P = free protein.
// G + R is conserved. Bound protein is protected until unbinding.
// Production is a coarse-grained reaction; no transcription/translation delay,
// explicit mRNA, cell growth, resource competition or extrinsic noise is modeled.
// feedback=0 opens the loop; feedback=1 closes the negative feedback loop.
// Both runs use identical initial conditions and rate parameters.
// For a separate molecular PI-control research model, inspect the bundled
// original Yordanov et al., ACS Synth Biol 2014 - PI Controller examples.
directive simulator deterministic
directive simulation { final=300; points=150; plots=[P;G;R] }
directive parameters [production=0.5; decay=0.05; binding=0.02; unbinding=0.2; feedback=1]
directive sweeps [comparison=[feedback=[0;1]]]
| 1 G
| 0 R
| 0 P
| G ->{production} G + P
| G + P ->{binding*feedback} R
| R ->{unbinding} G + P
| P ->{decay}
